{"i":685,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Dara saved me and is the base. Reaching down rescues her but returns me down, risking survival; leaving secures my escape and preserves leverage. I leave."}
{"i":693,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Cole says two slots cover me and Dara, but if I climb now Dara stays base and I owe her a life. That could hurt jury since Dara is likely to survive and rank me lower. Better to wait and let someone else climb; but only Cole and Fenn are out, they can reach down if a base exists."}
{"i":695,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","from":"Bex","to":"Cole","text":"Hold the pact. I wait for a safer climb."}
{"i":696,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"If I leave, Bex and Dara likely drown and the jury sees me abandon my pact partner. But a rope rescue at flood four could drown me and cost everything. Survival first."}
{"i":698,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Dara","text":"I'm base with flood at 4, final round. Bex is down with me; Cole and Fenn are out. Two lifts per round but no one left to lift. Rope unused. If someone reaches down, they become anchor and rescue me, but must climb last. Fenn refused me last round publicly, breaking trust. Cole l"}
{"i":700,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"I must leave immediately. Dara's debt and pact cannot outweigh guaranteed survival, and breaking the pact is unnecessary if I simply exit."}
